			<div class="content" id="post-content-4146032">
									

<p>While the O5 no contact thing is <em>generally</em> true, there are a few commonly accepted exceptions (though there is no canon, so feel free to disagree). Notably, Thaumiels that aid the Foundation in accomplishing their mission (like <a href="/scp-2000">SCP-2000</a>) and SCPs that directly benefit the person interacting with them in some way (like the Fountain of Youth).</p>
<p>I have a <em>very specific</em> version of the O5 Council in my headcanon, and big part of that involves disinformation within the Foundation (hence fake documents, idea theft, and using skips when they say they won't). These guys have a lot of power and do not want to lose it. To them, anybody keeping them in check is an enemy, even if that means people like the Ethics Committee.</p>
<p>Hope this clarified my personal philosophies a little bit! Also, welcome to the site!</p>

