			<div class="content" id="post-content-4147445">
									

<p>The argument can be made for keter, so maybe I'll tinker with the description to make this a clear safe class object. I'll isolate them to farms in the northeast atlantic or something. The point of my execution was to basically write a Series I magic animal as the cover up document, and then give it that modern twist in the level 4 version.</p>
<p>To answer how we found out about them, since they don't die and are all 100% identical to one another (and black), farmers would definitely notice that. Easterns are generally gray or cream colored, so a bunch of black ones would likely get tossed, and eventually the FDA would probably get called if a ton of black oysters kept showing up.</p>
<p>EDIT: Made it specify that the oysters can only reproduce with other anomalous oysters. Given the life cycle of oysters, this means they are exceedingly rare. Also explains why the bloom had to happen on a farm. Hope that alleviates the issue.</p>

